WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.907
A safer heap workflow starts with
intention.

2
00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:06.789
Allocate only after validating sizes,
initialize objects before use,

3
00:00:06.869 --> 00:00:10.036
and define the owner before returning or
sharing a pointer.

4
00:00:10.116 --> 00:00:13.854
A pointer value should travel with the
context needed to use it safely.

5
00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.595
Track bounds, ownership, and lifetime
together.

6
00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:19.146
Keep capacity and current length
consistent.

7
00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:21.126
Make ownership transfer explicit.

8
00:00:21.206 --> 00:00:25.514
Treat resizing and cleanup as state
transitions that can invalidate aliases and

9
00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:27.241
change what future code may do.

10
00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:29.222
Clean up predictably on every path.

11
00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:32.533
Success, failure, partial initialization,
early returns,

12
00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:36.034
and shutdown should all have
understandable release behavior.

13
00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:39.408
Free each allocation exactly once through
the correct owner,

14
00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:41.896
and do not use memory after its lifetime
ends.

15
00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:44.763
Finally, validate behavior with reviews
and tools.

16
00:00:44.843 --> 00:00:48.834
Ask who owns this heap object, how long it
remains valid, what bounds apply,

17
00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:53.096
what happens on allocation failure,
whether cleanup is correct on every path,

18
00:00:53.176 --> 00:00:56.660
and whether tests and diagnostics exercise
realistic behavior.
